# Force CRLF checkout for frozen B1a-5a study artifacts.
#
# DEV_PILOT_EXCLUSION_UNION.jsonl was originally written by
# dry_selection.py on Windows in text mode, so its on-disk line
# endings are CRLF. The SHA-256 of the CRLF file bytes is recorded
# inside every phase-checkpoint fingerprint AND in the manifest's
# exclusion_summary.union_ledger_sha256. That baked-in hash is the
# integrity anchor of the whole B1a-5a artifact chain.
#
# With eol=crlf, Git checks the file out with CRLF endings on every
# platform (Windows, Linux CI, macOS). sha256_file() then produces
# the same hash everywhere, matching what MANIFEST_V1 recorded.
# The blob itself stays LF-normalized internally; only checkout
# behavior is pinned.
#
# The .json and .md files are covered for the same reason: to keep
# every study artifact byte-stable across platforms even though only
# the JSONL is currently the subject of a raw-bytes SHA check.
docs/evaluation/DEV_PILOT_*.jsonl text eol=crlf
docs/evaluation/DEV_PILOT_*.json  text eol=crlf
docs/evaluation/DEV_PILOT_*.md    text eol=crlf
